# Known divergence, by design: multigres rejects CREATE FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER
# (Tier-2 — foreign data wrappers / foreign tables are not supported through the
# connection pooler; see go/services/multigateway/planner/unsafe_stmt.go). hastap
# builds an FDW inside a helper function (test_fdw) via a constant EXECUTE, so the
# gateway rejects that helper's CREATE FUNCTION; the missing helper then breaks the
# file's single wrapping transaction, truncating everything after it. That tail
# bundles the foreign-table assertions (has_foreign_table, has_relation on the
# foreign table) together with some general has_* checks the helper also emits
# (materialized view, partitioned table); all are lost together. The ~862
# assertions before the helper run and stay verified — including the general
# has_* functions on ordinary objects — so only these bundled instances are lost.
